<figure class="how-it-works" role="img" aria-labelledby="how-it-works-title" aria-describedby="how-it-works-desc how-it-works-alt">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 320" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100%" height="auto" role="presentation">
    <title id="how-it-works-title">How OpenFarm works</title>
    <desc id="how-it-works-desc">A place looks up a Köppen climate, which maps to one of 15 climate regions and their growing guides. Crop and variety facts, tools, and locally stored profile data sit alongside, all underpinned by sourced, licensed references.</desc>
    <style>
      .hw-n { fill: #e8f2e6; stroke: #2f6b3a; stroke-width: 1.5; }
      .hw-n2 { fill: #fff; stroke: #d9e3d6; stroke-width: 1.5; }
      .hw-core { fill: #2f6b3a; }
      .hw-t { font: 600 13px system-ui, sans-serif; fill: #1d2a1f; }
      .hw-tc { font: 600 13px system-ui, sans-serif; fill: #fff; }
      .hw-s { font: 12px system-ui, sans-serif; fill: #5d6b5f; }
      .hw-l { stroke: #2f6b3a; stroke-width: 1.25; fill: none; }
    </style>
    <line class="hw-l" x1="160" y1="160" x2="300" y2="160"/>
    <line class="hw-l" x1="460" y1="160" x2="600" y2="160"/>
    <line class="hw-l" x1="380" y1="70" x2="380" y2="108"/>
    <line class="hw-l" x1="380" y1="212" x2="380" y2="250"/>
    <line class="hw-l" x1="200" y1="70" x2="300" y2="120"/>
    <line class="hw-l" x1="560" y1="70" x2="460" y2="120"/>
    <rect class="hw-n2" x="20" y="28" width="180" height="56" rx="10"/>
    <text class="hw-t" x="110" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Your place</text>
    <text class="hw-s" x="110" y="70" text-anchor="middle">?place= city, or a map pin</text>
    <rect class="hw-n2" x="20" y="132" width="180" height="56" rx="10"/>
    <text class="hw-t" x="110" y="156" text-anchor="middle">Köppen climate</text>
    <text class="hw-s" x="110" y="174" text-anchor="middle">Beck et al. 2018, CC BY 4.0</text>
    <rect class="hw-core" x="300" y="108" width="160" height="104" rx="12"/>
    <text class="hw-tc" x="380" y="148" text-anchor="middle">15 climate regions</text>
    <text class="hw-s" x="380" y="168" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e8f2e6">one region for every place</text>
    <text class="hw-s" x="380" y="186" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e8f2e6">guides keyed to that climate</text>
    <rect class="hw-n" x="580" y="28" width="160" height="56" rx="10"/>
    <text class="hw-t" x="660" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Crops &amp; varieties</text>
    <text class="hw-s" x="660" y="70" text-anchor="middle">facts true everywhere</text>
    <rect class="hw-n" x="580" y="132" width="160" height="56" rx="10"/>
    <text class="hw-t" x="660" y="156" text-anchor="middle">Growing guides</text>
    <text class="hw-s" x="660" y="174" text-anchor="middle">/crops/…/&lt;region&gt;/</text>
    <rect class="hw-n" x="580" y="236" width="160" height="56" rx="10"/>
    <text class="hw-t" x="660" y="260" text-anchor="middle">Tools &amp; rotation</text>
    <text class="hw-s" x="660" y="278" text-anchor="middle">when a source supports it</text>
    <rect class="hw-n2" x="20" y="236" width="180" height="56" rx="10"/>
    <text class="hw-t" x="110" y="260" text-anchor="middle">Your profile</text>
    <text class="hw-s" x="110" y="278" text-anchor="middle">stays in this browser only</text>
    <rect class="hw-n2" x="300" y="236" width="160" height="56" rx="10"/>
    <text class="hw-t" x="380" y="260" text-anchor="middle">Sources &amp; licences</text>
    <text class="hw-s" x="380" y="278" text-anchor="middle">cited on every record</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption id="how-it-works-alt">
    <ol>
      <li>You choose a place (a readable <code>?place=</code> city link or a point on the map).</li>
      <li>OpenFarm looks up its Köppen–Geiger climate (Beck et al. 2018) in your browser and maps it to one of 15 climate regions.</li>
      <li>You get the growing guide for that region, when one exists, plus crop and variety facts that hold everywhere, and tools or rotation notes when a source supports them.</li>
      <li>Your profile, favourites and “what I’m growing” list stay in this browser — no account.</li>
      <li>Every record names its sources and follows the project’s licence rules.</li>
    </ol>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
